📘 Nested Virtualization on Azure
📌 Overview

This project demonstrates how to implement nested virtualization on Azure using Bicep and Custom Script Extension. An outer Azure VM acts as a hypervisor running KVM, which hosts an inner Ubuntu VM.

🏗 Architecture

Azure Resource Group

VNet + Subnet

NSG (SSH allowed)

Public IP (Static)

Outer VM (Standard_D4s_v3)

Custom Script Extension

KVM + libvirt

Inner Ubuntu VM

Shared folder via 9p

🚀 Deployment Steps
Step 1: Create Storage Account

Upload setup.sh script to private blob container.

Step 2: Secure Storage

Disabled public blob access.

Used protectedSettings in Custom Script Extension.

Step 3: Write Bicep Template

Included:

VNet

NSG

Public IP

NIC

VM

VM Extension

Step 4: Deploy
az deployment group create \
  --resource-group <rg-name> \
  --template-file twovm.bicep \
  --parameters @pm.json

🔐 Security Implementations

Storage account not public

Used protectedSettings for storage key

Parameterized secrets

Used environment().suffixes.storage

SSH restricted via NSG

🧪 Verification

SSH into outer VM:

ssh azureuser@<public-ip>


Check inner VM:

sudo virsh list --all


Get inner VM IP:

sudo virsh domifaddr inner-vm


SSH into inner VM:

ssh ubuntu@192.168.122.x

📂 Shared Directory Test

Inside inner VM:

echo "Hello" > /shared-data/test.txt


Inside outer VM:

cat /shared-data/test.txt